  "solution": {
    "approach": "Check if a year is a leap year using standard Gregorian calendar rules.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int y;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &y) == 1) {\n        if ((y % 400 == 0) || (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0)) {\n            printf(\"Leap Year\\n\");\n        } else {\n            printf(\"Not a Leap Year\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int y;\n    if (cin >> y) {\n        if ((y % 400 == 0) || (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0)) cout << \"Leap Year\\n\";\n        else cout << \"Not a Leap Year\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int y = sc.nextInt();\n            boolean isLeap = (y % 400 == 0) || (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0);\n            System.out.println(isLeap ? \"Leap Year\" : \"Not a Leap Year\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        y = int(s)\n        is_leap = (y % 400 == 0) or (y % 4 == 0 and y % 100 != 0)\n        print(\"Leap Year\" if is_leap else \"Not a Leap Year\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\n    if (s.length > 0) {\n        const y = parseInt(s, 10);\n        const isLeap = (y % 400 === 0) || (y % 4 === 0 && y % 100 !== 0);\n        console.log(isLeap ? \"Leap Year\" : \"Not a Leap Year\");\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "A year is leap if (y % 400 == 0) or (y % 4 == 0 and y % 100 != 0). Print 'Leap Year' or 'Not a Leap Year'."
  },
  "hints": [
    "Divisible by 400 is always leap.",
    "Divisible by 100 but not 400 is not leap.",
    "Divisible by 4 but not 100 is leap."
  ],
